From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 12:48:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] auth: ask Playport's host for Steam's auth session and web
 API tickets

In Playport the game runs in one process with the app that holds the
player's Steam session, and during a play the app keeps that session
logged on and makes the game's tickets as Steam's client does (Playport's
decision 0062). The emulator now asks it for them: a new playport_host
reaches the app through the Wine unix call table the runtime gives this
module (NtQueryVirtualMemory(MemoryWineLoadUnixLib) on its own image,
then __wine_unix_call), says hello once at start, and creates, polls and
cancels tickets by handle. Its protocol is fixed-size blocks with no
pointers, so the i386 build uses the same calls through WoW64.

The client's Auth_Manager (not the game server's) uses it:
GetAuthSessionTicket returns the host's ticket, bound to the
SteamNetworkingIdentity when the game passes a valid one, and posts
GetAuthSessionTicketResponse_t once Steam has taken it, a server refused
it, or 10 s passed; GetAuthTicketForWebApi does the same with its
identity and GetTicketForWebApiResponse_t; CancelAuthTicket takes a host
ticket out of Steam's list. The host's tickets are polled from
run_every_runcb, which the background thread also runs.

Where there is no such host (Windows, another Wine), or the play's
tickets are not armed, every call takes the made-up path as before.

Class: host-app
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-07-steam-live-session.md
Offered-upstream: no
